PATCH 583: extender op 0x60 -- the map stamps (8650, 8840, 88af) and the 32-bit app's EDX carried
across the service calls (ac70's exit).

board:0002.  The engine posts op 0x60 (e043: a world position and the two 16-byte image names
BURM_D2.KLC / BURM_C2.KLC in the TCB) for every burn mark of a mission -- 9cfc records one per
pre-placed wreck at mission setup, 9d26 replays the list, up to 32 -- and the service (10f1 = `call
8650`) presses the height image into the heightmap [0x85bc] and the colour image into the colormap
[0x85b8] around it.  None of 8650/8840/88af was in the decompile (the gate is their only caller); the
shim returned 0 for every post, so no mission's terrain carried its craters.  Transcribed from
0x8650-0x89a2 (fist_image.bin):

  8650   centre = ((x << 13) >> (32-DETAIL), (-y << 13) >> (32-DETAIL)); DETAIL < 9 -> -1; a flatness
         window of (2 * (4 << (DETAIL-9)) + 1) cells square: max - min of the heightmap > 9 -> -1;
         643c loads the height image into the 0x8644 scratch, bed2 x (10-DETAIL) or bc06 x
         (DETAIL-10) rescale it in place, the centre backs off by w/2, h/2 and 8840 presses it;
         the same again with the colour image, 4a3c, ac64 = [0x28a5], ac60 = 0xff, 88af.
  8840   cell = clamp0(pixel + cell - 0x80), byte arithmetic, columns wrapping on the mask, rows on
         the map size.
  88af   the pixel's own palette entry (643c leaves the image palette at 0x5598) is read for its G
         byte: 0x1f is transparent; else the cell's colour (the sorted map palette at 0x5260) is
         darkened (`shl bl,3` clear: * ((g & 0x1f) << 2 | 0x80) >> 8) or tinted (set: * ~((g & 0x1f)
         << 1) >> 8 + (g >> 1)) and ac70's nearest palette index replaces the cell.

  The window origin is `sub ebx,edx` / `sub ebp,edx` after `mov dl,4 ; shl dl,cl` -- only DL is set;
  the rest of EDX is whatever the previous service left in the app's register, which the extender
  preserves across its mode switches.  So the original's flatness test looks at the terrain 256*k
  cells away from the crater for k = bits 8..10 of that stale value: with 8650's own exit (ac70's
  best distance 0x3c1 or 0x2a4 after a pressed stamp, dh = 0 after a rejected one) the window moves
  by 784 or 528 cells for the next post.  A register trace of the oracle (tools/oracle/
  dosbox_blktrace.patch FIST_REGTRACE, scratch/oracle/regtrace*) shows exactly that at every one of
  AZER1's 16 posts, and -(y << 13) from the spawn's op-0x54 handler at the first.  The port carries
  it as g_ext_edx (tools/native_main.c): ac70's exit, 8650's paths, bed2/bc06, op 0x54.

  Measured: the port's height- and colormaps after AZER1's 16 posts are byte-identical to the
  oracle's (4 MB each, the live maps read through the extender's page tables); the 38 accept/reject
  decisions of AZER1, TRAIN2 and CYPRUS1 equal the oracle's.  A model without the stale EDX presses
  a crater at (388,1189) the original does not and skips the one at (620,201) it does.

